    equal: vs uniform guessing: LR-QAOA p = 2 raises P(cost <= 1.05 x optimum) per shot from 0.0005 to 0.0014 (2.9x); below uniform on 0 of 6 cases. The fairer random reference is the sampler with the target share (0.0005 per shot): LR-QAOA is 2.9x that, QAOA COBYLA 5.1x.
    equal: reliability: QAOA COBYLA (the standard choice, fixed in advance) gives an exact optimum with probability 0.0025 per shot and a split within 5 % with 0.0025; the best of 8 standard variants, picked AFTER seeing the results, is QAOA Powell with 0.0026.
    equal: vs classical, 1000 candidates each, probability of containing a split within 5 %: simulated annealing 0.65, local search 0.86 (+-0.03); LR-QAOA 0.76 -> BEHIND the best classical heuristic; QAOA COBYLA 0.92 -> ahead of it.
